A Description of the Liminal Union 🔰

The Liminal Union is an ancient commonwealth located south of the region that would
later become known as Wesnoth, on the far side of the Black River. Its land of hills,
green fields, and clean shores lies between the realms of western Elves, northern
Dwarves, eastern Dunefolk, and southern Drakes. For ages it has stood as a meeting-place
of roads, races, and ideas on the Great Continent.

Its people broke from the Elves in prehistory and chose to reject the rule of spellcraft
in mortal persons — whether learned by human magi, inherited through elvish bloodlines,
or cultivated in schools, grimoires, and necromantic arts. Through the Eighth-Day Severance —
a solemn purification using the medicinal minerals Zoelite and Akosite — each newborn child
is permanently untethered from the Faerie plane and anchored to mortal life. In place of
inherited magic they built a civic order based on law, compact, inquiry, and public obligation,
while holding the vampiric exiles of the Dark Forest to the strict border terms of the
Treaty of the Living and the Bound.

The Union is an egalitarian, anti-sorcerous commonwealth that exists in a perpetual flux
of change. It seeks a future in which birth, bloodline, superstition, and the private rule
of gifted spell-users no longer decide a person's fate. In this way, it strives to be a
light unto the nations of Irdya.

Instead of relying on sorcery, the Liminal Union developed alchemy, metallurgy, lawful
artifice, and the use of contained arcane forces in matter. From this tradition came Arcanite
and its companion alloys — fire-reactive Pyrite, heat-drinking Kryonite, conducting Uranite,
and purifying Zoelite and Akosite — used in weapons, armour, medicinal conduits, and bound cores. To many
foreigners this seems almost like sorcery, but the Union insists upon the distinction:
power bound in lawful vessels may serve the common good, while power wielded directly by
magi, necromancers, and blood-gifted castes corrupts judgment and endangers civic law.

Its armies are organised around four principal elements: the Maiden Corps, the Marine Corps,
G9 Quickbound Golems directed by Neural Curie Mainframes, and tamed Phoinix messenger birds. 
Together they form a combined-arms force that is mobile, disciplined by craft, and especially
dangerous to spell-users, necromancers, and other foes who trust in living magic.

When the people of the Green Isle came to the Great Continent, they brought with them the
pursuing Orcs and the shadow of the Lich-Lords. In the sealed records of Sayyon, the Ruby
of Fire was remembered as the Scarlet Faerie Stone affair. The diaspora intelligence
community of the Liminal Union had long watched this necromantic threat, and through
covert intervention helped keep it from returning to liches, necromancers, and the
walking dead.

Ancient, rational, and stubbornly free, the Liminal Union remains a threshold-civilisation:
standing between forest and sea, crown and desert, living spellcraft and the lawful
free & social civilization it has built against it.